            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "If we add an entity-manager member to the class (as private), we can avoid passing `io_context` and `objServer` or we implement all operations, which require direct io_context and objServer access, in entity-manager class, while keeping the interface related code here and call into the entity-manager functions.\n\nJust a thought."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Having an EM reference here could work but then we have the situation\nof circular references.\n\nSince EM has EMDBusInterface as a member.\n\nFor the intention of the patch, currently it is very simple as noted in the commit message.\n\nTo have a class to store ```inventory``` map and enable some functions to access it as before.\n\nThat change by itself is simple. If we get into OOP design with this change, it can be a long-winded discussion \ud83d\ude0a. So this patch is more of a keep it simple/stupid kind of patch.\n\nMaybe in your series you will get to a different abstraction which is better \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
